From 13e8146e30ab7d15b182a4f9e9ed600087b23ead Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rico Rojas <rickrojas@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 21:08:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] perf(dictation): open the pill and panel at once, warm
 the gate context, paste from the resident listener

Three more delays measured on the fork after the press path was fixed:

- The pill held 260 ms before growing (300 ms) and the live transcript
  entrance reached content ~1.5 s after the press. Both timelines keep
  their beats but land inside ~0.2 s and ~0.4 s respectively.
- The silence-gate AudioContext cost 135 ms on a cold audio stack every
  recording. It now survives the recording suspended and resumes in a
  few ms; cleanup() closes it.
- Spawning macos-fast-paste cost ~420 ms per paste, almost all of it a
  new process connecting to the window server. The resident Globe
  listener accepts a PASTE line on stdin and posts Cmd+V itself; the
  clipboard manager uses it when wired and falls back to the helper on
  any failure or timeout.
